  "notes": "USAGE:\nMost commonly used with する: {仕返|しかえ}しをする (to retaliate, to get revenge). More colloquial and everyday than {復讐|ふくしゅう} (vengeance), which implies deeper, more serious revenge.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {仕返|しかえ}しをする: to get revenge, to retaliate\n- {仕返|しかえ}しされる: to have someone get back at you\n- {仕返|しかえ}しを{恐|おそ}れる: to fear retaliation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{仕返|しかえ}し is more casual than {復讐|ふくしゅう} (vengeance) and {報復|ほうふく} (reprisal). {仕返|しかえ}し can be used for minor, everyday acts of getting even, while the others imply more serious or formal contexts.",
